HALO-VEIL CANTOR (CT04) — LANTERN ANIMATION TESTS
MOTION CONCEPT / CAMERA UNRESOLVED

Status
This pack is suitable for reviewing supernatural motion, silhouette, pacing and identity. It is not gameplay-view-ready. The required view is orthographic elevation 35.2643897 degrees, world azimuth 45 degrees, heading world +X / screen down-right. The generated art still reads nearer a frontal portrait despite the camera guide and a fresh camera/margin retry. Do not mistake prompt angle numbers for a verified projection.

Animations
- drift_veil_breath: six distinct drawings, 70 ticks at 60 Hz (1.1667 seconds). A gentle hover with expanding/closing veils, small drift and subtle halo/orb lag.
- resonant_spell: six distinct drawings, 90 ticks at 60 Hz (1.5 seconds). Rest, inward gathering, release, expanded tilted halo and angular ivory flare, ringing recoil, settle. Six drawings were chosen instead of the initial eight to protect the broad flare's silhouette and gutters.
- Two black hands, one brass orb and one coherent brass halo retained. The spell deliberately expands and tips that one halo; this is an intentional magical transformation.

