Native extraction and registration
All accepted generated sheets are 1448x1086 RGBA. Native pixels are preserved exactly. No frame is resized, mirrored, auto-fitted or independently recentered. Wide cels are isolated with generous non-overlapping source windows; they are placed using one fixed 1448/3 by 543-pixel source grid and the same output offset. The entire source alpha-positive pixel count is preserved exactly in the six extracted frames. All accepted source edges and output frame edges are clear of alpha >16.

Canvas/pivot
Every sprite frame is 640x640. Provisional review pivot is (328,595) from the top-left, normalized Unity-style bottom-left pivot (0.5125,0.0703125). This fixed canvas anchor is provided for playback; generated pose placement and apparent scale variation remain visible. No final world scale, collisions, hit events, sockets or gameplay camera calibration are asserted.

Timing
Drift hold ticks: 12,10,12,14,10,12. Preview repeats four times: 280 video frames, 4.6667 seconds.
Spell hold ticks: 20,14,8,14,10,24. Preview repeats three times: 270 video frames, 4.5 seconds. In use, play the spell once then return to a resting/hover state.

Provenance
Built-in image_gen used. Prompts include the user-requested words “Sunburst 2.5”. The tool does not expose a backend selection control or proof of which model served the request; no actual backend selection is claimed. All sheets are fresh generations from the original character reference and the deterministic camera guide, never an edit cascade.
Drift v01 was rejected for top-edge halo clipping and insufficient elevation. Drift v02 fixes complete silhouettes but does not solve the camera, and is retained only as a motion concept. Spell v01 is retained as a motion concept. No further drift generation or spell retry was used.

Review
Both source sheets and all ordered cels were inspected. Independent review confirmed the spell's one orb / one halo / two hands, coherent gather-offer-flare-recoil-settle sequence and no stray legs or feet. The floating orb in peak spell drawing 4 is preserved in extraction.

